var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"internal/","page":"Internal","text":"","title":"Internal"},{"category":"module","location":"internal/#BibInternal.BibInternal","page":"Internal","text":"BibInternal provides the canonical bibliography model shared by the bibliography stack.\n\nIt keeps the core entry types, validation rules, diagnostics, and lossless document containers in one place so parsers and exporters can share the same data model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.BibInternal"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.entries","page":"Internal","text":"const entries\n\nList of possible entries (currently based on bibtex). Keep it sorted for readability.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.entries"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.fields","page":"Internal","text":"const fields = [\n    :address,\n    :annote,\n    :archivePrefix,\n    :author,\n    :booktitle,\n    :chapter,\n    :crossref,\n    :edition,\n    :editor,\n    :eprint,\n    :howpublished,\n    :institution,\n    :isbn,\n    :issn,\n    :journal,\n    :key,\n    :month,\n    :note,\n    :number,\n    :organization,\n    :pages,\n    :primaryClass,\n    :publisher,\n    :school,\n    :series,\n    :title,\n    :type,\n    :volume,\n    :year\n]\n\nList of possible fields (currently based on bibtex). Keep it sorted for readability\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.fields"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.maxfieldlength","page":"Internal","text":"const maxfieldlength\n\nFor output formatting purpose, for instance, export to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.maxfieldlength"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.rules","page":"Internal","text":"const rules = Dict([\n    \"article\"       => [\"author\", \"journal\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"book\"          => [(\"author\", \"editor\"), \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"booklet\"       => [\"title\"]\n    \"eprint\"        => [\"author\", \"eprint\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"inbook\"        => [(\"author\", \"editor\"), (\"chapter\", \"pages\"), \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"incollection\"  => [\"author\", \"booktitle\", \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"inproceedings\" => [\"author\", \"booktitle\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"manual\"        => [\"title\"]\n    \"mastersthesis\" => [\"author\", \"school\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"misc\"          => []\n    \"phdthesis\"     => [\"author\", \"school\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"proceedings\"   => [\"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"techreport\"    => [\"author\", \"institution\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"unpublished\"   => [\"author\", \"note\", \"title\"]\n])\n\nList of BibTeX rules bases on the entry type. A field value as a singleton represents a required field. A pair of values represents mutually exclusive required fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.rules"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AbstractBibliographyRule","page":"Internal","text":"Base type for declarative and custom bibliography validation rules.\n\nThird-party packages may subtype this type and extend validate_rule without modifying BibInternal's canonical field model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AbstractBibliographyRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AbstractEntry","page":"Internal","text":"Abstract entry supertype.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AbstractEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Access","page":"Internal","text":"struct Access\n    doi::String\n    howpublished::String\n    url::String\nend\n\nStore the online access of an entry as a String. Handles the fields doi and url and the arXiv entries. For additional fields or entries, please fill an issue or make a pull request.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Access"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Access-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"Access(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the online access information based on the entry fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Access"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AlternativeRequiredField","page":"Internal","text":"AlternativeRequiredField(names)\n\nA requirement where at least one of the listed fields must be present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AlternativeRequiredField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.BibliographyDocument","page":"Internal","text":"BibliographyDocument\n\nLossless document-level container returned by parsers that need to preserve ordering, non-entry blocks, and parse diagnostics.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.BibliographyDocument"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Date","page":"Internal","text":"struct Date\n    day::String\n    month::String\n    year::String\nend\n\nStore the date information as day, month, and year.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Date"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Date-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"Date(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the date information based on the entry fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Date"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Diagnostic","page":"Internal","text":"Diagnostic\n\nStructured message attached to a bibliography document, raw entry, or field. The suggestion field is intentionally textual for now so command line tools and future GUIs can present a friendly next action without depending on a fix engine.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Diagnostic"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.DiagnosticSeverity","page":"Internal","text":"@enum DiagnosticSeverity diagnostic_info diagnostic_warning diagnostic_error\n\nSeverity level for structured diagnostics emitted while parsing, normalizing, or validating bibliography data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.DiagnosticSeverity"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Entry","page":"Internal","text":"struct Entry <: AbstractEntry\n    access::Access\n    authors::Names\n    booktitle::String\n    date::Date\n    editors::Names\n    eprint::Eprint\n    id::String\n    in::In\n    fields::Dict{String,String}\n    note::String\n    title::String\n    type::String\nend\n\nGeneric Entry type. If some construction rules are required, it should be done beforehand. Check bibtex.jl as the example of rules implementation for BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"Entry(id::String, fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct an entry with a unique id and a list of Fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Entry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.EntryRule","page":"Internal","text":"EntryRule\n\nValidation rule for one source entry type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.EntryRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.EntryRuleSet","page":"Internal","text":"EntryRuleSet\n\nVersioned collection of entry validation rules for a bibliography format. The aliases dictionary applies before entry-specific aliases, which makes it easy to share canonical field names across the whole format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.EntryRuleSet"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Eprint","page":"Internal","text":"struct Eprint\n    archive_prefix::String\n    eprint::String\n    primary_class::String\nend\n\nStore the information related to arXiv eprint format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Eprint"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Eprint-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"Eprint(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the eprint arXiv information based on the entry fields. Handle old and current arXiv format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Eprint"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldCardinalityRule","page":"Internal","text":"FieldCardinalityRule(name, minimum=0, maximum=nothing)\n\nConstrain the number of values in a structured field. Flat string values count as one; parsers that preserve multiple values should pass a collection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldCardinalityRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldSpec","page":"Internal","text":"FieldSpec\n\nFormat-independent description of a canonical bibliography field. Parsers and exporters own source-format mappings; this catalog only describes the semantic field exposed to downstream consumers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldSpec"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldTypeRule","page":"Internal","text":"FieldTypeRule(name, value_kind)\n\nRequire a populated field to match a canonical value kind such as :integer, :year, :date, or :uri.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldTypeRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Fields","page":"Internal","text":"Fields = Dict{String, String}. Stores the fields name => value of an entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Fields"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.ForbiddenField","page":"Internal","text":"ForbiddenField(name)\n\nReject a field when it has a value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.ForbiddenField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.In","page":"Internal","text":"struct In\n    address::String\n    chapter::String\n    edition::String\n    institution::String\n    isbn::String\n    issn:String\n    journal::String\n    number::String\n    organization::String\n    pages::String\n    publisher::String\n    school::String\n    series::String\n    volume::String\nend\n\nStore all the information related to how an entry was published.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.In"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.In-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"In(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the information of how an entry was published based on its fields\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.In"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.LosslessEntry","page":"Internal","text":"LosslessEntry\n\nPair a stable canonical Entry with the raw source entry and diagnostics used to build it. This keeps existing consumers on Entry while enabling parsers and writers to preserve source information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.LosslessEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.MutuallyExclusiveFields","page":"Internal","text":"MutuallyExclusiveFields(names)\n\nAllow at most one populated field in the group.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.MutuallyExclusiveFields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Name-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"Name(str::String)\n\nDecompose without ambiguities a name as particle (optional) last, junior (optional), first middle (optional) based on BibTeX possible input. As for BibTeX, the decomposition of a name in the form of first last is also possible, but ambiguities can occur.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Name"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawBlock","page":"Internal","text":"RawBlock\n\nTop-level source block that is not necessarily a bibliographic entry, such as a BibTeX comment, preamble, string definition, or free text.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawBlock"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawEntry","page":"Internal","text":"RawEntry\n\nLossless representation of a parsed bibliography entry. kind is the source entry type, key is the citation key when the format has one, and fields preserves source order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawField","page":"Internal","text":"RawField\n\nLossless representation of a parsed field.\n\nname and value contain the interpreted field pair, while raw preserves the source representation. span and diagnostics are optional metadata collected by parsers that keep source locations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RequiredField","page":"Internal","text":"RequiredField(name)\n\nA single required field in an entry rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RequiredField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RuleContext","page":"Internal","text":"RuleContext\n\nContext passed to validate_rule. Custom rule packages can extend validate_rule(rule, fields, context) for their own AbstractBibliographyRule subtype.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RuleContext"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RuleProfile","page":"Internal","text":"RuleProfile\n\nNamed and versioned set of composable bibliography rules. A nothing supported_entry_types value means that the profile accepts every entry type; it is used for product or institution overlays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RuleProfile"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.SourceSpan","page":"Internal","text":"SourceSpan\n\nOptional source location for raw bibliography content and diagnostics. The span uses 1-based inclusive coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.SourceSpan"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.ValidationResult","page":"Internal","text":"ValidationResult\n\nResult of validating one entry or a bibliography document. ok is true when no diagnostic has diagnostic_error severity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.ValidationResult"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#Base.isless-Tuple{BibInternal.Date, BibInternal.Date}","page":"Internal","text":"Base.isless(a::BibInternal.Date,b::BibInternal.Date)::Bool\n\nFunction to check for a < b on BibInternal.Date data types.\n\nThis function will throw an ArgumentError if the year can not parsed into Int. If it is not possible to parse month or day to Int those entries will be silently ignored for comparison. This function will not check if the date fields are given in a correct format all fields are parsed into and compared as Int (no checking if date format is correct or valid!).\n\ndanger: Note:\nThe silent ignoring of not parseable month or day fields will lead to misbehaviour if using comparators like == or !==!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isless"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#Base.isless-Tuple{BibInternal.Name, BibInternal.Name}","page":"Internal","text":"Base.isless(a::BibInternal.Name,b::BibInternal.Name)::Bool\n\nFunction to check for a < b on BibInternal.Name data types.\n\nThis function will check the fields last, first and middle in this order of priority. The other fields are ignored for now. The field comparison is done by string comparison no advanced alphabetizing rules are used for now.\n\ndanger: Note:\nThe silent ignoring of the other fields might lead to misbehaviour if using comparators like == or !==!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isless"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.arxive_url-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"arxive_url(fields::Fields)\n\nMake an arxiv url from an eprint entry. Work with both old and current arxiv BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.arxive_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.canonical-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"Internal","text":"canonical(entry)\n\nReturn the canonical Entry view of an entry-like object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.canonical"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.canonical_field_specs-Tuple{}","page":"Internal","text":"canonical_field_specs()\n\nReturn the canonical field catalog in stable display order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.canonical_field_specs"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.check_entry-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"check_entry(fields::Fields)\n\nCheck the validity of the fields of a BibTeX entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.check_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.compose_profiles-Tuple{Vararg{BibInternal.RuleProfile}}","page":"Internal","text":"compose_profiles(profiles...; name)\n\nCompose format, product, and institution profiles. Constraints accumulate. Conflicts are retained as error diagnostics on the resulting profile rather than being resolved through precedence.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.compose_profiles"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.diagnostics-Tuple{BibInternal.LosslessEntry}","page":"Internal","text":"diagnostics(entry)\n\nReturn the diagnostics attached to a lossless entry or document.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.diagnostics"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.entry_fields-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"Internal","text":"entry_fields(entry::Entry)\n\nConvert a canonical Entry back into a flat field dictionary. This is the bridge used by validation and format conversion code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.entry_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.erase_spaces-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"erase_spaces(str::String)\n\nErase extra spaces, i.e. r\"[  ]+\", from str and return a new string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.erase_spaces"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.field_spec-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internal","text":"field_spec(name)\n\nReturn the canonical specification for name, or nothing for a source-specific extra field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.field_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.get_delete!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"get_delete!(fields::Fields, key::String)\n\nGet the value of a field and delete it afterward.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.get_delete!"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.handle_validation-Tuple{BibInternal.ValidationResult, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"handle_validation(result::ValidationResult, level)\n\nApply a validation policy. :error raises on errors, :warn logs warnings, and :none returns the result untouched.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.handle_validation"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.make_biblatex_entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"make_biblatex_entry(id::String, fields::Fields; check = :error)\n\nMake an entry using BibLaTeX field aliases and date conventions while preserving source-specific fields that are not part of the canonical view.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.make_biblatex_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.make_bibtex_entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internal","text":"make_bibtex_entry(id::String, fields::Fields)\n\nMake an entry if the entry follows the BibTeX guidelines. Throw an error otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.make_bibtex_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.names-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"names(str::String)\n\nDecompose into parts a list of names in BibTeX compatible format. That is names separated by and.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.names"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.profile_field_names-Tuple{BibInternal.RuleProfile, AbstractString}","page":"Internal","text":"profile_field_names(profile, entry_type)\n\nReturn fields made available by the profile for an entry type. Custom fields remain legal unless a profile explicitly forbids them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.profile_field_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.profile_rules-Tuple{BibInternal.RuleProfile, AbstractString}","page":"Internal","text":"profile_rules(profile, entry_type)\n\nReturn global rules followed by rules for the normalized entry type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.profile_rules"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.raw-Tuple{BibInternal.LosslessEntry}","page":"Internal","text":"raw(entry)\n\nReturn the raw source representation attached to a lossless entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.raw"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.space-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internal","text":"space(field::Symbol)\n\nReturn the amount of spaces needed to export entries, for instance to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.space"},{"category":"function","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate","page":"Internal","text":"validate(entry::Entry, ruleset::EntryRuleSet = BIBTEX_RULESET)\n\nValidate a canonical entry against a ruleset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"function","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate-2","page":"Internal","text":"validate(entry::LosslessEntry, ruleset::EntryRuleSet = BIBTEX_RULESET)\n\nValidate the canonical view of a lossless entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate-Tuple{BibInternal.BibliographyDocument, BibInternal.EntryRuleSet}","page":"Internal","text":"validate(document::BibliographyDocument, ruleset::EntryRuleSet)\n\nValidate every entry stored in a lossless bibliography document.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, BibInternal.EntryRuleSet}","page":"Internal","text":"validate_fields(fields::AbstractDict, ruleset::EntryRuleSet; id::AbstractString = \"\")\n\nValidate one field dictionary against a ruleset and return structured diagnostics. The input dictionary can come from a parser or from a canonical entry converted back to fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, BibInternal.RuleProfile}","page":"Internal","text":"validate_fields(fields, profile; id=\"\")\n\nValidate one entry against a composed rule profile.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate_fields"},{"category":"section","location":"bibtex/","page":"BibTeX","text":"The BibTeX parser is the core parser shipped with BibParser.jl.\n\nIt accepts both plain BibTeX and BibLaTeX syntax, and it can return either the legacy entry dictionary or a lossless document model.\n\n","title":"BibTeX"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Accumulator","page":"BibTeX","text":"mutable struct Accumulator\n\nA structure to accumulate part of the input stream as a simple string. It differs from Position that store line and column information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Accumulator"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.BibTeXError","page":"BibTeX","text":"BibTeXError\n\nDescription of a BibTeXError, including the relevant position in the input string.\n\nArguments:\n\nkind::Symbol: the type of BibTeX error\ninput::String: the BibTeX string being parsed\nstart::Position: the row/col start position of the BibTeXError\nstop::Position: the row/col end position of the BibTeXError\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.BibTeXError"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Content","page":"BibTeX","text":"Content\n\nStore the different BibTeX elements once successfully parsed.\n\nwarning: Note:\nFree text, comments entries and preambles entries are currently ignored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Content"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Content-Tuple{}","page":"BibTeX","text":"Content()\n\nCreate an (almost) empty content constructor for a new Parser. Some usual BibTeX content is added:\n\nList of months abbreviations in English (added automatically by some BibTeX class)\n\nFeel free to contribute to more default content.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Content"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Field","page":"BibTeX","text":"Field\n\nA structure that can store BibTeX fields information.\n\nArguments:\n\nbraces::Int: counter to the number of opened braces in a field being parsed\nname::String: name of the field being parsed\nquotes::Bool: true if the field is delimited by quotes\nvalue::String: the value of the field\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Field"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Parser","page":"BibTeX","text":"Parser\n\nA structure allowing to parse a BibTeX formatted string one character at a time.\n\nArguments:\n\nacc::Accumulator: an accumulated string from last dump to content\ncontent::Content: the current content of a parser\nerrors::Vector{BibTeXError}: a collection of BibTeX errors\nfield::Field: temporary storage for an entry fields names\ninput::Vector{Char}: the BibTeX string\npos_start::Position: pointer to the raw/col start position\npos_end::Position: pointer to the raw/col end position\nstorage::Storage: temporary storage of the content of an entry being parsed\nrules_checker::Bool: indicate which level :error, :warn, or :none should be raised when an entry violates BibTeX rules\nformat::Symbol: bibliography ruleset used for canonical entry construction\ntask::Symbol: describe which part of the BibTeX gramma is being parsed\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Parser"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Position","page":"BibTeX","text":"Position\n\nA structure pointing to a position in the input based on rows and columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Position"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Position-Tuple{}","page":"BibTeX","text":"Position()\n\nInitial position constructor\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Position"},{"category":"type","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Storage","page":"BibTeX","text":"Storage\n\nStore the content of an entry being parsed.\n\nArguments:\n\ndelim::Union{Char, Nothing}: the character delimiting the entry\nfields::Vector{Field}: a collection of the entry's fields\nkey::String: the key of the entry\nkind::String: the kind/type of BibTeX entry\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Storage"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.Storage-Tuple{}","page":"BibTeX","text":"Storage()\n\nEmpty storage constructor called when a new entry is being parsed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.Storage"},{"category":"function","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.dump!","page":"BibTeX","text":"dump!(parser, char = ' ')\n\nDump the content of the parser Accumulator into the parser Content. Dispatch to the appropriate dump! method according to the state of the parser.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.dump!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.finalize_entry!-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"finalize_entry!(parser)\n\nFinalize the current parsed entry and store it in parser content. Duplicate keys are handled according to parser rules_checker:\n\n:error: throw an error\n:warn: emit a warning and keep first occurrence\n:none: silently keep first occurrence\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.finalize_entry!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.get_acc-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"get_acc(parser; from = 1, to = 0)\n\nRetrieve the Accumulator of the parser.\n\nArguments:\n\nparser: a Parser\nfrom: a positive offset from the start of the Accumulator, default to 1\nto:  a negative offset from the end of the Accumulator, default to 0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.get_acc"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.get_entries-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"get_entries(parser)\n\nRetrieve the entries successfully parsed by parser.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.get_entries"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.inc!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"inc!(parser, char, dumped)\n\nIncrement the start/end position and accumulator of the parser.\n\nArguments:\n\nparser: a BibTeX.Parser structure\nchar: the character being parsed\ndumped: boolean value describing if the Accumulator content is being dumped into the parser Content\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.inc!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.inc_col!-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"inc_col!(parser) = begin\n\nIncrement the column field of the pointer to the end position of the Parser.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.inc_col!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.inc_row!-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"inc_row!(parser)\n\nIncrement the row field of the pointer to the end position of the Parser.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.inc_row!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.is_dumped-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"is_dumped(parser, char)\n\nCheck if an Accumulator needs to be dump!ed. Dispatch to the appropriate is_dumped method according to the state of the parser.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.is_dumped"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.make_entry-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"make_entry(storage)\n\nMake a BibInternal.Entry from a completed entry in a parser storage.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.make_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.parse!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"parse!(parser, char)\n\nParse a single character of a BibTeX string. Modify the Parser accordingly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.parse!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.parse_file-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"parse_file(path)\n\nParse a BibTeX file located at path. Raise a detailed warning for each invalid entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.parse_file"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.parse_string-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"parse_string(str)\n\nParse a BibTeX string of entries. Raise a detailed warning for each invalid entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.parse_string"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.rev-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"rev(char)\n\nReturn the closing character )/} matching either ( or {.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.rev"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.set_delim!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"set_delim!(parser, char)\n\nSet the delimiter for this section of the entry to parenthesis or braces.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.set_delim!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.set_entry_kind!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"set_entry_kind!(parser, kind) = begin\n\nSet the kind of the entry being parsed in the parser's storage.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.set_entry_kind!"},{"category":"method","location":"bibtex/#BibParser.BibTeX.warn-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibTeX","text":"warn(error)\n\nDispatch a BibTeX error as a Julia warning based on the type of error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibTeX.warn"},{"category":"section","location":"","page":"BibParser","text":"BibParser turns bibliographic source text into canonical bibliography entries or lossless bibliography documents.\n\nUse it when you need parsing only. Use Bibliography.jl when you want the full import/export workflow.\n\nSupported formats:\n\nBibTeX and BibLaTeX in the core package;\nRIS in the core package;\nCFF 1.2 through the YAML and JSONSchema extensions;\nCSL-JSON through the JSON3 extension;\nEndNote XML and MODS through the EzXML extension.\n\nThe lossless document parser keeps raw blocks, source spans, and diagnostics when the backend format makes that possible.\n\nusing BibParser\n\nentries = parse_file(\"references.bib\")\ndocument = parse_bibliography(\"references.bib\"; format = :BibTeX)\n\n","title":"BibParser"},{"category":"module","location":"#BibParser.BibParser","page":"BibParser","text":"BibParser converts bibliography source formats into BibInternal data.\n\nThe package focuses on parsing only. Use parse_entry and parse_file for the legacy entry dictionary workflow, or parse_bibliography when you want a lossless BibInternal.BibliographyDocument.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibParser"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.detect_format-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"detect_format(input)\n\nBest-effort format detection used by parse_bibliography when format = :auto.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.detect_format"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.detect_xml_format-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"BibParser","text":"detect_xml_format(content::AbstractString)\n\nHeuristic XML format detection used by the parser extensions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.detect_xml_format"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.parse_bibliography-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_bibliography(input; format::Symbol = :auto, check = :error)\n\nParse a bibliography and return a BibInternal.BibliographyDocument preserving raw source blocks where the parser supports lossless mode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_bibliography"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.parse_entry-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_entry(entry::String; parser::Symbol = :BibTeX, check = :error)\n\nParse a single BibTeX entry string using the legacy parser.\n\nFor bibliography formats with validation rules, the check keyword argument can be set to :none, nothing, :warn, or :error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.parse_file-Tuple{Any, Val{:BibTeX}}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_file(path::String, parser::Symbol = :BibTeX; check=:error)\n\nParse a bibliography file and return the legacy entry representation.\n\nThe default parser is :BibTeX. Use :BibLaTeX or :RIS directly in the core package, and install the relevant extensions to enable the other formats. For bibliography formats with validation rules, check can be :none, nothing, :warn, or :error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_file"},{"category":"method","location":"#BibParser.parse_string-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_string(input::String; format::Symbol = :BibTeX, check = :error)\n\nParse bibliography content from a string and return entries in the legacy format. Prefer parse_bibliography when source preservation and diagnostics are needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_string"},{"category":"section","location":"csl/","page":"CSL-JSON","text":"\n\nBibParser supports CSL-JSON through the JSON3 extension. This parser maps CSL records onto the canonical BibInternal.Entry model and keeps the original JSON payload in the lossless document view.\n\nusing BibParser, JSON3\n\ndocument = parse_bibliography(read(\"references.json\", String); format = :CSL)","title":"CSL-JSON"}]
}
